Quoting from a separate email conversation:

"I have been working on the data and have part of the skyline files ready. I tried to visualize those in MSstatsShiny <https://msstatsshiny.com/app/MSstatsShiny>, but there was a file size limitation of 250mb, while my files were closer to 500mb. I was able to surpass the limit by running MSstatsShiny on my laptop, but now when I try to upload the files, MSstatsShiny just seems to load forever. I believe the files are too big for the program. Have you heard of this problem? Have you any ideas for refining the data or otherwise reducing the file size?"

If anyone has any issues uploading files on MSstatsShiny on your laptop, there may be two potential problems:
You may have ran out of RAM space: this could occur if you're running other applications.  I know on Windows, you can halt those applications on Task Manager.
You ran out of space in your temporary files folder: I know on Windows, you can check the Disk Cleanup application and delete "Temporary files".
Tony

